From the double angle formulas, $\sin x = 2 \sin \frac{x}{2} \cos \frac{x}{2}$ and $\cos x
= 2 \cos^2 \frac{x}{2} - 1 = 1 - 2 \sin^2 \frac{x}{2},$ so \begin{align*} \ensuremath{\frac{1 + \sin x
- \cos x}{1 + \sin x + \cos x}} \&= \ensuremath{\frac}\{1 + 2 \ensuremath{\sin} \ensuremath{\frac{x}{2}} \ensuremath{\cos} \ensuremath{\frac{x}{2}} - 1 + 2
\ensuremath{\sin}\^{}2 \ensuremath{\frac{x}{2}}\}\{1 + 2 \ensuremath{\sin} \ensuremath{\frac{x}{2}} \ensuremath{\cos} \ensuremath{\frac{x}{2}} + 2 \ensuremath{\cos}\^{}2 \ensuremath{\frac{x}{2}} - 1\} \\
\&= \ensuremath{\frac}\{2 \ensuremath{\sin} \ensuremath{\frac{x}{2}} \ensuremath{\cos} \ensuremath{\frac{x}{2}} + 2 \ensuremath{\sin}\^{}2 \ensuremath{\frac{x}{2}}\}\{2 \ensuremath{\sin} \ensuremath{\frac{x}{2}}
\ensuremath{\cos} \ensuremath{\frac{x}{2}} + 2 \ensuremath{\cos}\^{}2 \ensuremath{\frac{x}{2}}\} \\ \&= \ensuremath{\frac}\{2 \ensuremath{\sin} \ensuremath{\frac{x}{2}} (\ensuremath{\cos} \ensuremath{\frac{x}{2}}
+ \ensuremath{\sin} \ensuremath{\frac{x}{2}})\}\{2 \ensuremath{\cos} \ensuremath{\frac{x}{2}} (\ensuremath{\sin} \ensuremath{\frac{x}{2}} + \ensuremath{\cos} \ensuremath{\frac{x}{2}})\} \\ \&=
\ensuremath{\frac}\{\ensuremath{\sin} \ensuremath{\frac{x}{2}}\}\{\ensuremath{\cos} \ensuremath{\frac{x}{2}}\} \\ \&= \ensuremath{\boxed}\{\ensuremath{\tan} \ensuremath{\frac{x}{2}}\}. \end{align*}
